# Resume assigned queue (#3605 / #3611)

Always-on ticks must re-read discovered work. `fresh=0` is not idle when the resume queue is non-empty (`/tmp/lgfc-cursor-resume-queue.json`).

An item is *waiting* when:

- its linked open authored PR has latest checks SUCCESS (independent review or merge approval), or
- it is `handoff:ready` (labels/status only — not website Go)

`nextExecutable` is the highest-ranked resume-queue item that is not waiting. After a PR is opened, a HOLD is posted, or PACKAGE-INCOMPLETE is recorded, immediately continue `nextExecutable`:

1. Numbered Operations interrupts that still need a Cursor action
2. Assigned open Issues that are not merely waiting on review
3. Open authored PRs with failing or pending gates
4. Cursor-owned `post-merge-failure`
5. `agent:cursor` + `status:active` that is not merely waiting on review

If `nextExecutable` is absent, keep looping for follow-through on waiting items. Do not idle and do not self-merge.

Waiting is follow-through only. Do not occupy the session with standing-queue status. Interrupt a waiting item when gates fail, a reviewer comments, or a Cursor-owned closeout exception opens.

Do not mix remaining queue items into the just-opened PR. `handoff:ready` is not website Go. Do not self-merge.

Canonical: `docs/ops/ai/CORE-RULES.md` assigned-queue continuation.
